// Prologue: The Edge. Story bible section 7.0. Wren and Isolde at the Greyfold's edge at dusk.
// The tutorial is characterisation. Isolde speaks plainly (style guide section 6, the exception).
// Beats are started by PrologueDirector from flags; nodes end where the player has to do something.
// Commands: <<flag>>, <<tutorial>>, <<bind_prompt>>, <<cutscene>> (PRG-08, PRG-16).

title: Prologue_Edge_Arrive
---
<<flag prologue.started 1>>
Isolde: Stop. Here is far enough. #face:wary #line:0dc8c94
Isolde: Tell me what you see, journeyman. #face:asking #line:01f262b
-> White. It's closer than last month. #line:07682d7
    <<voice surveyor greyfold>>
    Isolde: Nine wingspans closer. I measured. #plant:4.6 #line:04b5965
-> The Half-Cathedral. Its bells are still up. #line:0e30177
    <<voice warden greyfold>>
    Isolde: They ring, some nights. Nobody's inside to ring them. #plant:6.12 #face:grave #line:0ee1f1d
-> Nothing. I can't look straight at it. #line:0b08369
    <<voice drift greyfold>>
    Isolde: No one can. That's the first thing to learn about the Blank. Look beside it. #line:0f1ba9b
Isolde: We'll take a page of it before dark. Then I'll show you something. #face:bright #line:091e9b6
<<tutorial survey>>
Isolde: The marker, there. The lens. Slow. Let the pen find the line; don't push it. #line:08422cf
===

title: Prologue_Edge_Survey
---
Isolde: There. Feel the page take it? #face:bright #line:050623e
Isolde: Now bind it. A page without a memory is only a drawing. #line:082e77c
<<bind_prompt isolde.first_sight>>
Isolde: I'll give you mine. Write it exactly. #line:0337489
Isolde: "A child at the edge of the white, looking straight at me. The only one who could." #plant:5.3 #line:0d48af4
-> Me. #line:0f19008
    <<voice warden greyfold>>
    Isolde: You. Six years old and not afraid of it. I was terrified. #face:bright #line:0a8c928
-> Why that memory? #line:041eb6d
    <<voice surveyor greyfold>>
    Isolde: Because it's the truest thing I own. Binding wants the truest thing. #line:0897e78
-> ... #line:0913f86
    <<voice drift greyfold>>
    Isolde: Quiet suits a cartographer. Seal it. #face:bright #line:08d671d
<<tutorial seal>>
<<flag prologue.sealed_edge_page 1>>
<<jump Prologue_Edge_Dusk>>
===

title: Prologue_Edge_Dusk
---
Isolde: Good. That's the last thing I can teach you standing still. #face:bright #line:0789e28
<<tutorial strike>>
Isolde: Smudges come out at dusk here. Quill up. Strike where the ink is thickest. #line:024f22c
Isolde: I'll take the near ones. The last is yours. Only when it's there to hit. #line:0fa4bcb
===

title: Prologue_Edge_AfterSmudges
---
<<flag prologue.first_smudges 1>>
Isolde: You hold it like Voss taught you. Loosen your wrist. #plant:5.5 #line:0e1c170
<<jump Prologue_Edge_Departure>>
===

title: Prologue_Edge_Departure
---
Isolde: Wren. #face:grave #line:024564b
Isolde: I'm going in. #face:grave #line:034c888
-> You don't have a tether. #line:05a31b4
    <<voice warden greyfold>>
    Isolde: No. #face:grave #line:053ae88
-> Then I'm coming. #line:058346f
    <<voice drift greyfold>>
    Isolde: You'll try. That's rather the point. #plant:5.2 #face:bright #line:02c5444
-> Why? #line:0e7b6a1
    <<voice surveyor greyfold>>
    Isolde: Because I drew something I shouldn't have. And because someone in there is owed a visit. #plant:5.2 #face:grave #line:096dd5c
Isolde: Don't anchor what I've drawn. Come find why. #face:grave #line:02124a5
Isolde: Look at me. Only at me. Then look beside the white. #plant:5.3 #face:grave #line:06c0854
<<cutscene edge_departure>>
<<flag prologue.isolde_entered 1>>
===

// Isolde when pressed up on between beats. The director starts the beats themselves.
title: Prologue_Edge_Idle
---
<<if not has_flag("prologue.sealed_edge_page")>>
    Isolde: Beside it, journeyman. The marker's behind you. Slow. #still #line:03f853b
<<elseif not has_flag("prologue.first_smudges")>>
    Isolde: Quill up. They're only ink. Strike when they're thickest. #still #line:0ed8901
<<else>>
    <<jump Prologue_Edge_Departure>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Prologue_Shore_Wake
---
// Saltmarrow shore. Wren wakes. Sable stands over her.
Sable: Wings high, stranger. You've come a long way to be lost. #face:bright #line:0d9bb77
Sable: Guild cowl. No licence on you. No atlas either. Three torn pages and a quill. #face:wary #line:09043f9
-> Where is this? #line:0b878ca
    <<voice surveyor saltmarrow>>
    Sable: The Saltmarrow. The far side of everything. The Blank spat you out here; it does that, sometimes. #line:0d3e9b5
-> How long was I gone? #line:0646920
    <<voice drift saltmarrow>>
    Sable: Long enough that the Guild's stopped looking. A fortnight, by the tide. #line:0f30252
-> There was a kite. Isolde Marr. #line:0d9153a
    <<voice warden saltmarrow>>
    Sable: Nobody came out but you. Nobody ever comes out. #plant:5.2 #face:grave #line:0dfe5fa
Sable: Quay's up the boardwalk. Everything there has a price. Including me. #face:bright #line:02553ba
<<flag prologue.torn_pages 3>>
<<flag saltmarrow.met_sable 1>>
<<flag prologue.woke_on_shore 1>>
<<flag act1.started 1>>
<<clock dawn>>
===
